        "content": "## Dragon v2 — idempotent, authorized, non-destructive labels\n\n- Sender must be in the allowlist (currently: repo owner only).\n- opened/labeled/reopened matrix enforced in code; every other action and every non-matching label is rejected and logged.\n- commandVersion = issue.updated_at (GitHub-native, stable across redeliveries, changes on genuine retries).\n- Lock is acquired via Supabase POST with Prefer: resolution=ignore-duplicates — atomic at the database level, not a check-then-write race.\n- Status labels are added/removed individually via the GitHub REST API, never replacing the full label array — unrelated labels (bug, priority, ...) are preserved.\n- Every received event is logged to dragon_events_log regardless of outcome.\n- Renamed role: Executive Intake & Drafting Assistant. No execution tools. Every posted comment carries a fixed, non-model-generated disclaimer.\n\nNOT YET VALIDATED BY A LIVE IMPORT/RUN. See docs/DRAGON_DEPLOYMENT_RUNBOOK_AR.md before activating.",
